  "id": "2026-09-17-suggestions-editing-visibility",
  "scope": "suggestions",
  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-09-17",
  "question": "How can playground and editor-ai default to direct editing while keeping existing pending suggestions visible and reviewable?",
  "model": "GPT-6 / Codex",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v2 with redesign-from-first-principles and maximum-value hard-cut comparison",
  "trigger": "User screenshot shows missing pending insertions after the default editing-mode repair; user explicitly requests Best API Review.",
  "requirements": [
    "Default to direct edits while existing pending insertions, deletions and other reviewable changes remain visible.",
    "Changing typing intent must not implicitly decide suggestions or hide pending work.",
    "Keep canonical accepted content, retained changes, authorship, dependencies and atomic decisions in one native authored owner.",
    "Keep view policy and selection local to the exact mounted lifetime, with correct caret, paste, history and persistence behavior.",
    "Preserve explicit accepted-only views for independent preview/export jobs without imposing product defaults on all raw Plite consumers."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Rechecked the September 14 initialization decision, current EditorViewOptions union, setAuthoredView validator, updateView and finishContent coordinate/publication choices, BaseSuggestionPlugin presets, both real editor roots and browser assertions. Earlier receipt outcomes remain historical; no old browser pass is reused as proof of the newly required combined behavior.",
  "summary": "Pursue deleting the coupling between write intent and displayed projection at the native authored view/transaction owner. Keep EditorRoot initialization and native authored authority; propose edit/markup for general editors and intent-only mode changes. Current APIs cannot express the required behavior, and changing types or CSS alone cannot repair transaction coordinates.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": "2026-09-14-suggestions-view-initialization-api",
  "relation": "supersedes",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep/configure existing modes: rejected. edit/accepted hides pending insertions; propose/markup creates new proposals. edit/markup is excluded by the public union and runtime validator.",
    "Change the existing native contract: selected direction. Admit direct writes in a review-visible projection with explicit native coordinate and publication semantics. Plate adopts that capability at EditorRoot and removes the projection reset from mode controls; no extra mode store or wrapper.",
    "Add a primitive: no new public noun is currently justified. The missing capability belongs to existing authored view and transaction contracts, with mapping internals private. Exact behavior inside or across retained work remains design work.",
    "Delete or merge: remove the intent/projection equivalence and preset coupling. Deleting SuggestionPlugin alone cannot remove the native restriction and would relocate its independent human review and decoration job. Keep Comments independent.",
    "Move ownership to app paint, CSS, a plugin effect or switch/edit/restore handler: rejected. Omitted insertion content and proposed coordinates cannot be restored by styling; temporary view switches add selection, IME and transaction hazards.",
    "Replace native authored storage or accept proposals for visibility: rejected for this job. Acceptance changes user data and decisions; parallel retained content or a second suggestion engine duplicates existing authority. No evidence requires replacing storage before evaluating the native contract repair."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Bounded source assessment plus supplied screenshot codex-clipboard-ab1aedfb-4849-43c4-af04-4f886ff0a46e.png. No product edits, new runtime experiment, browser replay, performance measurement or general suggestion audit. The current validator explicitly rejects the proposed combination. Design must prove edits before/inside/across pending content without silent acceptance or attribution loss, retained-deletion behavior, structural/property edits, paste, native caret, undo/redo, save/reload and exact-view independence. Prior heading-only typing proof did not assert pending visibility. Earlier hydration and paint failures remain unresolved; this review does not establish they are unrelated.",
